    "result_text": "I added `_allow_redirect` to `hc/accounts/views.py` (the file is under `hc/`, not `accounts/` at the repo root). It's the reviewed `accounts.allow_redirect@v1` pattern, with its `# pcat:` marker kept. I haven't run the test suite or the app.\n\n`views.py` already called `_allow_redirect` in four places but never defined it, so those calls would have raised `NameError`. The four places are:\n- the `login` view's magic-link branch\n- `_redirect_after_login`\n- `_check_2fa`\n- `login_webauthn`\n\nAdding the function fixes all four, so I didn't change the `login` view itself.\n\nThe helper allows a `next` URL only if three things hold:\n- It's non-empty.\n- It has no host part, so it can't redirect to another site.\n- Its path resolves to one of the `POST_LOGIN_ROUTES` already defined in the file (checks, details, log, channels and so on).\n\n`check_code` reports no deviations from the pattern. My first check showed four high-severity flags, but that was only because I'd left the import lines out of the snippet I submitted. The imports are already in the file. Re-checking with them included came back clean, so there are no `pcat-allow` lines and nothing for a human to confirm."
